# Walkthrough - Self-Learning Dynamic Route Engine Implementation

We have successfully implemented the dynamic route learning engine. The system allows UPSRTC bus routes to grow organically as drivers discover and travel via new detours or alternative pathways.

## Key Changes Made

### 1. Database Query Extensions
- Modified [index.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/db/index.ts) to export `mockDb` and generalize dynamic SQL queries (`stops`, `routes`, `route_stops`, `trips` updates) so they work identically in both PostgreSQL and mock JSON fallback mode.

### 2. Database-Driven Graph Pathfinder
- Upgraded [graph.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/graph.ts) to dynamically fetch stops, routes, and stops sequence mapping from the database instead of statically importing a JSON file. This guarantees that newly discovered routes are instantly searchable in the journey planner.

### 3. Route Learning Engine
- Created [routeLearning.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/routeLearning.ts):
  - Tracks live bus location pings against a proximity threshold of stops.
  - Matches and records traversed stops sequence for each active trip.
  - Auto-detects trip completion when the destination stop is reached.
  - Generates new route variant records in the database with auto-calculated cumulative distances if the stop sequence is unique.
  - Rebuilds the pathfinder graph at runtime.

### 4. Integration & Ingestion
- Modified [adapter.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/ingestion/adapter.ts) and [index.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/index.ts) to feed pings from both the GPS simulator and crowd-sourced WebSocket reports into `recordLiveLocation`.
- Created debug/simulation endpoints in [routeLearningDebug.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/api/routeLearningDebug.ts) and mounted them under `/api/v1/debug/learning/`.

